; SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

; =============================================================================
; SheetsApp — the Ranger spreadsheet core with an EVGUI interface around it
; =============================================================================
;
;   ┌─ header ── EVGSheets · File Edit View Insert Format Data ── book.xlsx ─┐
;   ├─ ribbon ── ↶ ↷ │ Font▾ 11▾ │ B I U S A▁ ◩▁ │ ≡ ≡ ≡ ↵ ⊞ │ $▾ % │ … ──┤
;   │ ┌─ the core (GridApp): formula bar, headers, cells, dialogs ─────────┐ │
;   │ │                                                                    │ │
;   │ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
;   ├─ footer ── Sales  Costs  Summary  + ─────────── Sum 4,100 · Count 201 ─┤
;   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
;
; Two worlds, one canvas. The CORE is gallery/datagrid's GridApp: the workbook
; model, the formula engine, xlsx in and out, the grid, the formula bar and
; every dialog — the editor that has the features. The INTERFACE is EVGUI: a
; menubar, dropdown menus, a ribbon of icon toggles, tabs and a context menu,
; each one an EVGUI controller in a UiHost, styled by one stylesheet
; (sheets.css) with a light and a dark palette.
;
; The seam is the display list. The page is laid out by EVG; the element with
; id `sx-grid` is a placeholder whose rectangle is handed to GridApp as its
; window, and GridApp's own list is painted INTO that element with
; `EVGDisplayList.paintAt` — so a menu that drops over the grid is drawn over
; it, and the grid's own dialogs stay inside the grid.
;
; The two halves agree on state by asking, never by mirroring: a toggle on the
; ribbon is ON because `GridFormat` says the active cell is bold, read again
; after every input. The ribbon does not remember Bold; it reports a press and
; the core decides.
;
; The accessibility trees merge the same way the pictures do: the chrome's
; tree from UiHost, the core's from GridApp, the core's hung under a region
; node at the grid's rectangle. One tree, one focus.
;
; It runs PARAMETRISED: `setPreset("full" | "compact" | "viewer" | "grid")`
; and `setOption(name value)` choose which pieces are shown, which ribbon
; tools exist, and whether the workbook can be edited at all — the same editor
; as a full application, as a light viewer inside another app, or as a bare
; grid.
; =============================================================================

